<h2 style="font-size:13pt;margin:16pt 0 6pt;">I. Introduction</h2><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;">the Defendant, by and through counsel, respectfully submits this Motion to Suppress in the matter of Evidence Test, Case No. EV-1783523382. Exclude evidence obtained in violation of the defendant’s constitutional rights.</p><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;">This motion is brought pursuant to Cal. Penal Code § 1538.5; U.S. Const. amend. IV; Cal. Const. art. I, § 13. Counsel must confirm the applicability of each authority to the facts of this case.</p><h2 style="font-size:13pt;margin:16pt 0 6pt;">II. Statement of Facts</h2><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;">1/5/2026, 3:00:00 PM: Incident reported at the residence (4th &amp; Main).</p><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;">1/5/2026, 3:20:00 PM: Officer arrived on scene.</p><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;">Witness statement taken (time unknown).</p><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;">The following evidence is on file and forms part of the record: witness.txt.</p><h2 style="font-size:13pt;margin:16pt 0 6pt;">III. Procedural History</h2><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;"><b>[ATTORNEY INPUT REQUIRED] </b>Procedural history is not available from the repository. Counsel must supply the procedural history.</p><h2 style="font-size:13pt;margin:16pt 0 6pt;">IV. Applicable Law</h2><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;">The controlling authority for a Motion to Suppress is: Cal. Penal Code § 1538.5; U.S. Const. amend. IV; Cal. Const. art. I, § 13. Counsel must confirm current applicability and jurisdiction.</p><h2 style="font-size:13pt;margin:16pt 0 6pt;">V. Analysis</h2><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;"><b>[ATTORNEY INPUT REQUIRED] </b>The repository does not currently contain findings that independently support this Motion to Suppress. Counsel must supply the legal argument and identify the supporting facts and authorities.</p><h2 style="font-size:13pt;margin:16pt 0 6pt;">VI. Conclusion</h2><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;">For the foregoing repository-supported reasons, the Defendant respectfully requests that this Court suppress the challenged evidence and any fruits thereof. Counsel affirms that the factual assertions herein are drawn from the case repository and that any matters marked UNKNOWN require independent verification before filing.</p><h2 style="font-size:13pt;margin:16pt 0 6pt;">VII. Prayer for Relief</h2><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;">WHEREFORE, the Defendant respectfully prays that this Court suppress the challenged evidence and any fruits thereof, and grant such other and further relief as the Court deems just and proper.</p><h2 style="font-size:13pt;margin:16pt 0 6pt;">VIII. Certificate of Service</h2><p style="margin:0 0 8pt;text-align:justify;"><b>[ATTORNEY INPUT REQUIRED] </b>I hereby certify that on [DATE — UNKNOWN], a true and correct copy of the foregoing was served upon [RECIPIENT — UNKNOWN] by [METHOD — UNKNOWN]. Counsel must complete this certificate before filing.</p>

